[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 968,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138161,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Optic nerve choristoma is a rare, benign, and probably developmental/malformative choristomatous lesion composed of smooth muscle and adipose tissue within and around the optic nerve.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138162,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138163,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LA13.7Y Other specified congenital malformation of optic disc</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138164,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138165,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138166,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is equal left:right optic nerve involvement. The location within the nerve may be intracanalicular, intraorbital, and intracranial involving the optic chiasm {11987274}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138167,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is a painless, slow, progressive decrease in visual acuity, associated with optic atrophy. In rare cases, the visual loss may be rapid and progressive. MRI shows enlargement of the nerve and hyperintense signal that disappears with fat suppression, suggestive of a fat-containing lesion. Differential diagnostic considerations may include optic nerve glioma, optic nerve meningioma, lipoma, an inflammatory process, and a secondary process involving the optic nerve {28774539}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138168,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Rare single case reports in the literature show an approximately equal sex distribution and an age range from 9&nbsp;to 63&nbsp;years.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138169,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138170,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This is believed to be a developmental malformation with heterotopic smooth muscle and adipose tissue within and around the optic nerve. Optic disc colobomas may be associated with heterotopic adipose tissue and/or smooth muscle {6847467}. A rare case showed mixed features of both optic nerve coloboma and morning glory anomaly.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138171,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Optic nerve choristoma may appear as a yellow/tan mass.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138172,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Histology shows adipose tissue and bundles of smooth muscle in variable amounts within or adjacent to atrophic optic nerve tissue. Immunohistochemistry for SMA highlights the smooth muscle component, and GFAP staining highlights optic nerve tissue {11987274;15806516;28774539;29755281}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 744,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138173,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 744,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Limited experience</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 980,
